        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Golden Temple</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1581 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Made by</span><span class="info-stat-val">Begun by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guru-arjan">Guru Arjan</a>, the fifth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> Guru, on a pool completed by Guru Ram Das; rebuilt by Sikhs after repeated destruction, and rebuilt in marble and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Maharaja Ranjit Singh</a>, who overlaid the sanctum with gold leaf</span></div>
